>> title: Split Pea Soup
>> category: Soups
>> tags: peas, ham, stovetop, make-ahead
>> counters: Diner, Deli, One Pot
>> aka: pea soup, split pea and ham, green split pea soup
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 30 min
>> washing-up: the soup pot
>> keeps: 4 days — it sets like a mousse cold and loosens with stock, and the smoke off the hock comes forward

>> step: sweat 8 min
Sweat @yellow onion{1%large}, @carrots{2%medium}, and @celery{2%ribs} in @unsalted butter{2%Tbs} for ~{8%min}.

>> step: simmer 1 hr 15 min, shred the hock
Simmer @&(~1)vegetables{} for ~{75%min} with @green split peas{1%lb}(450 g), @smoked ham hock{1}, @chicken stock{8%cups}(1.9 L; plus water as it thickens), and @bay leaf{1}, then pull the meat off the bone and stir it back in.

>> step: mash coarse
Mash @&(~1)soup{} to a coarse purée with a #potato masher{}.

Season @&(~1)soup{} with @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp}, and @cider vinegar{1%tsp}.
